{"_data": [{"contents": [{"content": "New Paths", "type": "lesson_name"}, {"content": "Family Life", "type": "unit_name"}, {"content": 8, "type": "position"}, {"content": "stub", "type": "origin"}, {"content": 1, "type": "lesson"}, {"content": "B1.1", "type": "level"}], "type": "metadata"}, {"contents": [{"content": "false", "type": "test"}], "type": "achievment_test"}, {"contents": [{"content": "Describe routines and regular activities in a wider range of social and work contexts.", "type": "primary"}, {"content": "Writes short texts about presenting plans for a future activity at work using correct spelling, grammar, cohesion and coherence aspects appropriate to the communicative functions for this level.", "type": "secondary_1"}, {"content": "Writes short texts about presenting plans for a future activity at work using correct spelling, grammar, cohesion and coherence aspects appropriate to the communicative functions for this level.", "type": "secondary_2"}, {"content": "Writes short texts about presenting plans for a future activity at work using correct spelling, grammar, cohesion and coherence aspects appropriate to the communicative functions for this level.", "type": "secondary_3"}, {"content": "Writes short texts about presenting plans for a future activity at work using correct spelling, grammar, cohesion and coherence aspects appropriate to the communicative functions for this level.", "type": "secondary_4"}, {"content": "Writes short texts about presenting plans for a future activity at work using correct spelling, grammar, cohesion and coherence aspects appropriate to the communicative functions for this level.", "type": "secondary_5"}, {"content": "Writes short texts about presenting plans for a future activity at work using correct spelling, grammar, cohesion and coherence aspects appropriate to the communicative functions for this level.", "type": "secondary_6"}, {"content": "Writes short texts about presenting plans for a future activity at work using correct spelling, grammar, cohesion and coherence aspects appropriate to the communicative functions for this level.", "type": "secondary_7"}, {"content": "Writes short texts about presenting plans for a future activity at work using correct spelling, grammar, cohesion and coherence aspects appropriate to the communicative functions for this level.", "type": "secondary_8"}], "type": "objectives"}, {"content": "engenn6le01ob08re1img01.jpg", "type": "background_image"}, {"contents": [{"content": "Writing about Family", "type": "heading"}, {"content": "When you are writing about your family, there are a number of items to include. <br><br>First: Introduce yourself. Include your name, age and where you are from. <br><br>Second: Include the rest of your family members (your immediate family and extended family.  Sometimes a person can have a blended family).", "type": "describer"}, {"content": "{\"rows\":4,\"columns\":2,\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Family Members\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" Example\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Immediate family\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">mother, father, sister, brother</span> \\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Extended family\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">aunt, uncle, cousin</span> \\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Blended family\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">half-sisters, half-brothers</span> \\\"}\"],\"styles\":\" instruction_table_background intro_table_border\"}", "type": "table"}, {"content": "I have two half-sisters. This is my father's second marriage.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "I have a large extended family.", "type": "example"}], "type": "learning_points"}, {"contents": [{"content": "Rhetorical Questions in Writing", "type": "heading"}, {"content": "Rhetorical questions are questions that you don't answer. You ask rhetorical questions in order to make a point about a situation or to point out something.", "type": "describer"}, {"content": "{\"rows\":5,\"columns\":2,\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Types of Rhetorical Questions\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" Example\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Big life questions\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">Aren't we just tiny pieces in a big picture?</span> \\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" Questions that draw attention to something\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">Do you know what time it is? - meaning it's late</span> \\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Questions to express a bad mood\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">What's the point in trying?</span> \\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Questions that point to a positive\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">Didn't  I help you on your last exam?</span> \\\"}\"],\"styles\":\" instruction_table_background intro_table_border\"}", "type": "table"}, {"content": "You can use the structure How + adjective/adverb to ask rhetorical questions. This way, you can ask a question that gets people to think about what you are writing about. ", "type": "text"}, {"content": "How much time does it take to become successful?", "type": "example"}, {"content": "How much do you really know about your family members?", "type": "example"}, {"content": "How well do you really know yourself?", "type": "example"}, {"content": "How close are you really to your family?", "type": "example"}, {"content": "How crazy are we?", "type": "example"}], "type": "learning_points"}, {"contents": [{"content": "unexpectedly", "type": "name"}, {"content": "not expected or planned", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(adverb)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: One of my weaknesses is that I am not very flexible.  When situations change unexpectedly, it is a real challenge for me.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn6le01ob08aud01", "type": "audio"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"content": "These are words you use to describe family relationships.", "type": "text"}], "type": "target_word_describer"}, {"contents": [{"content": "realist", "type": "name"}, {"content": "a person who accepts and deals with things as they really are", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: I consider myself to be a realist.  ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn6le01ob08aud02", "type": "audio"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"content": "face value", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to accept someone or something just as it appears", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(expression)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example:  I take things at face value ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn6le01ob08aud03", "type": "audio"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"content": "flexible", "type": "name"}, {"content": "willing to change or to try different things", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(adjective)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: One of my weaknesses is that I am not very flexible.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn6le01ob08aud04", "type": "audio"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"content": "immediate family", "type": "name"}, {"content": "close family members including brothers, sisters, and parents", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: My immediate family includes two older brothers. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn6le01ob08aud05", "type": "audio"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"content": "blended family", "type": "name"}, {"content": "a family consisting of a couple and their children from this and all previous relationships", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: I come from a blended family; this is my father's second marriage. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn6le01ob08aud06", "type": "audio"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"content": "half-sister", "type": "name"}, {"content": "a sister with whom one has only one parent in common", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: They are my half-sisters, Camilla and Roseanne.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn6le01ob08aud07", "type": "audio"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"content": "impulsive", "type": "name"}, {"content": "acting or done without much thought", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(adjective)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: Camilla tends to be a little too impulsive.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn6le01ob08aud08", "type": "audio"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"content": "slopes", "type": "name"}, {"content": "hills for skiing", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: How impatient is Roseanne going to be on the slopes?", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn6le01ob08aud09", "type": "audio"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"content": "quick-tempered", "type": "name"}, {"content": "easily made angry", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(adjective)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: Roseanne is quick-tempered.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn6le01ob08aud10", "type": "audio"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"content": "Interview a partner or friend about their family.  Do they have a small family? Large, extended family? Blended family?", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Ask your partner to describe their personalities.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Write a 75-100 word paragraph about their family.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Read the paragraph aloud.", "type": "text"}], "type": "takeaway_extension"}, {"contents": [{"content": "I interview a friend or partner about their family.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I describe people's personalities.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I write a paragraph about a family.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I read my paragraph about a family aloud.", "type": "text"}], "type": "takeaway_assessment"}], "labs": [{"stimuli": [{"contents": [{}], "template_override": 1, "_data": [], "id": 0, "type": "welcome"}, {"template_override": 1, "_data": [], "title": "", "type": "audio", "contents": [{"value": {"images": [{"image": "engenn6le01ob08re2img01.jpg", "time": "0", "id": 0, "text": ""}, {"image": "engenn6le01ob08re2img01.jpg", "time": "100", "id": 1, "text": "I'm going to tell you about my family. My name is Isabelle Richardson. I'm twenty-five years old and from San Diego, California. I consider myself to be a realist.  I take things at face value and am honest with my feelings.  One of my weaknesses is that I am not very flexible.  When situations change unexpectedly, it is a real challenge for me. My immediate family includes two older brothers who are at a prestigious university, Sean and Luca. How clever are they to be at a famous university? They are arriving from New York tonight for the holidays."}, {"image": "engenn6le01ob08re2img02.jpg", "time": "38000", "id": 2, "text": "I come from a blended family; this is my father's second marriage.  He had two children with his first wife.  They are my half-sisters, Camilla and Roseanne. We are always excited to see each other. However, we all have different personalities. Camilla tends to be a little too impulsive while Roseanne is quick-tempered."}, {"image": "engenn6le01ob08re2img03.jpg", "time": "62000", "id": 3, "text": "Christmas gatherings are always an experience! This year, we  will be heading to the snow! <br><br>How impatient is Roseanne going to be on the slopes? How crazy are we?"}], "audiosrc": "engenn6le01ob08re2aud01", "coverimg": "engenn6le01ob08re2img01.jpg"}, "type": "slideshow"}], "id": 1}, {"template_override": 1, "_data": [], "title": "", "type": "video", "contents": [{"value": {"images": [{"image": "", "time": "0", "id": 0, "text": "Introduce yourself and your family<br>\n<ul><li>What is your name?</li>\n<li>Who is part of your immediate and extended family?</li>\n<li>Do you have a blended family?</li></ul>"}], "video_src": "engenn6le01ob08re3vid01"}, "type": "video"}], "id": 2}], "exercises": [{"template_override": 1, "_data": [{"contents": [{"content": " I can write about family life and personal qualities.", "type": "Learning Outcomes"}, {"content": " I can ask questions about how people are. ", "type": "Learning Outcomes"}, {"content": " I can write about future action, plans and intentions.", "type": "Learning Outcomes"}, {"content": " Describe your family. How many uncles, aunts, and cousins do you have?", "type": "Free Header Item"}, {"content": " Do they have different personalities? What are they like?", "type": "Free Header Item"}], "type": "instructions"}, {"contents": [{"content": "Welcome", "type": "group_name"}], "type": "group"}, {"content": {"correct_feedback": "Correct", "incorrect_feedback": [{"content": "try again", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Maybe next time", "type": "text"}], "attempt_feedback": [{"content": "You have 2 tries", "type": "text"}, {"content": "you have 1 attempt left", "type": "text"}], "allowed_attempts": 2}, "type": "feedback"}, {"content": "Ask your partner:", "type": "free_header_text"}, {"content": "Writing Spot: Who is Isabelle Richardson?", "type": "free_type_text_area"}], "questions": [], "type": "WLC", "id": 0, "img_path": "", "stimuli_ids": [0]}, {"template_override": 1, "_data": [{"contents": [{"content": "Isabelle talks about 